# Build intermediates.
# Directory.Build.props sends them to obj/ and bin/ beside each Source/, outside Mod/: they
# must never end up back inside Mod/, which is uploaded to the Workshop whole, as-is.
Tests/Pickle/Source/obj/
Tests/Pickle/Source/bin/
Source/obj/
Source/bin/

# Claude Code working directory. It used to be covered by the machine's global ignore file, a
# property of the machine and not of the repository: this repository now carries the rule itself.
.claude/

# Development environments
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.csproj.user

# Windows Explorer folder icons. desktop.ini is listed under System below. Art/ModIcon.ico and
# Art/Preview.ico are publishable outputs (PUBLISHING.md, "Jeu minimal de sources et sorties") and are tracked;
# an .ico anywhere else, above all in Mod/ (Steam receives it as it is), never belongs in the repository.
*.ico
!Art/ModIcon.ico
!Art/Preview.ico

# Compiled DirectDraw textures. RimWorld loads a .dds in preference to the .png beside it, so a stale
# one silently overrides the texture that was edited. Derived files: never versioned. Written twice
# because the patterns are not case-folded and the files on disk come out uppercase.
*.dds
*.DDS

# Test evidence: Pickle reports and captures. Kept on disk only, one latest report per scenario and
# per revision, and it can grow to gigabytes. What is versioned is one text line per run in
# docs/runs/. See "What to keep after a test" in TESTING.md.
Tests/Pickle/Evidence/
evidence/
# System
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Reproducible Preview diagnostics generated locally by the shared renderer.
Art/.render/
Tests/Pickle/Inbox/
Tests/Pickle/Parked/
